Phases, diffusion and solidification — Cambridge DoITPoMS (@mat-doitpoms-phases: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_4HHCB32507KCQ5FPHGT4JD5GTB
University of Cambridge, Department of Materials Science and Metallurgy. Read the complete [Phase Diagrams and Solidification](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/phase-diagrams/index.php), [Ternary Phase Diagrams](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/phase3_diagrams/index.php), [Diffusion](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/diffusion/index.php) and [Solidification of Alloys](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/solidification_alloys/index.php) packages with their questions.

These illustrated lessons connect free energy and composition balances to observations and transport. Use their conditions explicitly when comparing a simple model with real processing. The ternary package includes sections, tie triangles and a Sn–Ag–Cu case; the solidification package covers partitioning, Scheil, zone refining and morphological stability.

Indexes and selected free-energy, lever-rule, Fick-law, interdiffusion and Scheil pages were directly retrieved and read on 30 October 2026, despite web-preview 403 responses. Live simulations and every linked activity were not all exercised. The inspected footer states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 except where otherwise noted; preserve contributor and third-party credits. Read externally; do not import the whole collection or assume a downloadable figure lacks separate rights.

